==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|honestly}}, {{m|enm|honestlyche}}, {{m|enm|honestliche}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|honest|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɑnɪstli/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɒnɪstli/}}
* {{hyph|en|hon|est|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|manner}} In an [[honest]] manner.
#: {{usex|en|He answered the questions '''honestly'''.}}
# [[frankly|Frankly]], [[to be honest]].
#: {{usex|en|'''Honestly''', I didn't believe a word she said.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|honest manner}} {{l|en|candidly}}, {{l|en|sincerely}}, {{l|en|truthfully}}; see also [[Thesaurus:honestly]]
* {{sense|frankly}} {{l|en|as a matter of fact}}, {{l|en|in point of fact}}, {{l|en|in truth}}; see also [[Thesaurus:actually]]

